 ### [4D Gaussian Rasterization](13946-4d-gaussian-rasterization.md)
-Renders 4D Gaussians (3D spatial + 1D temporal) into a 2D image for a specific viewpoint and timestamp. It extends static 3D Gaussian Splatting by handling time-dependent opacity, position offsets, and spherical harmonics evaluation in 4D. Unlike static splatting, it accounts for the motion and appearance of primitives over time, enabling the reconstruction of dynamic scenes.
+Renders 4D Gaussians (3D spatial + 1D temporal) into a 2D image for a specific viewpoint and timestamp. It extends static 3D Gaussian Splatting by handling time-dependent opacity, position offsets, and spherical harmonics evaluation in 4D. Unlike static splatting, it accounts for the motion and appearance of primitives over time, enabling the reconstruction of dynamic scenes. Choose this method when rendering time-varying scenes; otherwise, use the static 3D Gaussian Splatting method.
 
